      "Heat a heavy skillet over medium-high heat. Sear the chicken for 5-7 minutes per side until deeply browned and cooked through (165°F/74°C internal). Remove the chicken and set aside, leaving the drippings and browned bits in the pan.",
      "Reduce the heat to medium-low. Whisk the egg yolk and milk together, then pour into the skillet with the drippings along with the chipotle chili powder, oregano, basil, and turmeric.",
      "Simmer the sauce, stirring constantly, for 3-4 minutes until it thickens enough to coat the back of a spoon. Scrape up any browned bits from the bottom of the pan as it reduces.",
